url: "https://github.com/dada8899/structural-isomorphism"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dada8899/structural-isomorphism"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  A Clauset-grade analysis pipeline for cross-domain validation of self-
  organized criticality (SOC), preferential attachment, and adjacent
  universality classes (Motter-Lai network cascade, Preisach hysteresis,
  Scheffer fold bifurcation, aggregation kinetics, Schelling credible
  commitment, Pythia LAMBADA scaling). One shared ~339-LOC Python module
  (v4/lib/soc_pipeline.py) applied unchanged across nineteen empirically-
  anchored universality classes plus synthetic null controls. v0.5
  introduces three methodology increments (§3.6.5 (s*, k) threshold-
  tobit reparametrisation; §3.6.6 multilayer test pattern; §3.6.7 head-
  vs-tail-aware LLM validator), promotes one new class
  (aggregation_kinetics, PASS-STRONG across 3 distinct biological
  domains), and reports an eval-specific TIGHT_UNIVERSALITY finding for
  Pythia LAMBADA scaling (CV ≈ 0.12 within-eval; CV ≈ 0.58–1.49 cross-
  eval). Includes a B1/B3 multi-model LLM ensemble critic over a 21-
  candidate universality-class taxonomy, frozen pipeline source, and
  213+ tests across unit / integration / e2e tiers. Companion preprints
  (paper/v0-unified-pipeline-2026-05-13.md and the v0.5 draft skeleton
  at paper/v0.5-draft/v05-draft-skeleton.md) ship in the same
  repository.
keywords:
